            "text": "General precautions",
            "level": "h2",
            "anchor": "precautions"
          }
        },
        "content_2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<ul><li>An oral device doesn't replace a diagnosis or treatment from a healthcare provider.</li><li>Using these appliances for a long time can change the way your teeth fit together.</li><li>If you feel pain in your jaw, teeth or ear, stop using the device and talk to a healthcare provider or dentist.</li><li>If you have braces, dentures or dental implants, or problems with your jaw joint, check with your dentist first.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
